<title>UK: Ex-dividends take 1.015 off UK's FTSE 100 index.</title>
<headline>Ex-dividends take 1.015 off UK's FTSE 100 index.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>FTSE International said the following FTSE 100 stocks went ex-dividend on Monday and the effect was to take 1.015 points off the index in early trading.</p>
<p>						 DIVIDEND   INDEX</p>
<p>						 (PENCE)    EFFECT</p>
<p>		COMPANY			  Net	 Net</p>
<p>	  * Associated British Foods    4.25	0.218</p>
<p>	  * Reuters Holdings		3.10	0.299</p>
<p>	  * Scottish &amp; Newcastle	 14.17	0.498</p>
<p>	-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7954</p>
</text>
